sentences.text:
Having heard the submissions made at the Bar and after going through materials available in the record, it is pertinent to mention here that the essential ingredients to constitute the offence punishable under Section 498A of IPC are - (i) a woman was married;
(ii) she was subjected to cruelty;
(a) by any willful conduct which is of such a nature that is likely to drive a woman to commit suicide, or to cause grave injury or danger to life, limb, whether mental or physical health of a woman; or [ 2025:JHHC:18674]
(b) by harassing a woman where such harassment is with a aim of coercing her or any person related to her to meet any unlawful demand for any property or for any valuable security or is on account of failure by her or any person related to her to such demand.

